R31 — drop the hardcoded `OpenAI-Beta: realtime=v1` header from LiteLLM's
OpenAI realtime WebSocket leg.

⚠️  STATUS — PARTIAL / DEFENSE-IN-DEPTH ONLY
============================================
This patch removes the `OpenAI-Beta` header from
`OpenAIRealtime._get_additional_headers` — the header source the R31
investigation originally identified. LIVE VERIFICATION (debug session
r31-realtime-ga-shape) PROVED THIS IS INSUFFICIENT: LiteLLM 1.83.14's
actual OpenAI realtime WS path still sends `OpenAI-Beta: realtime=v1`
from a DIFFERENT, un-traced code path, and OpenAI still answers
`beta_api_shape_disabled`. The bundled `litellm` realtime backend
therefore CANNOT complete an OpenAI Realtime GA session on 1.83.14.

The supported, verified-working path is the `direct` realtime backend
(`REALTIME_BACKEND=direct`, now the DEFAULT) — the Fastify relay connects
straight to OpenAI's GA `/v1/realtime`, bypassing LiteLLM. This patch is
retained as defense-in-depth: it is correct as far as it goes, and if a
future LiteLLM release routes the OpenAI realtime leg through
`_get_additional_headers`, the patch closes the header there. Track
LiteLLM for a proper OpenAI Realtime GA release before relying on the
`litellm` backend.

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS
=====================
OpenAI retired the Realtime *Beta* API. Its GA `/v1/realtime` surface
rejects any connection that carries the `OpenAI-Beta: realtime=v1` header
(or the Beta-only `?intent=` query param) with
`invalid_request_error.beta_api_shape_disabled`, closing the socket 4000.

LiteLLM 1.83.14's `OpenAIRealtime._get_additional_headers()` returns that
header UNCONDITIONALLY for every `openai/` realtime model. There is no
config knob, no `extra_headers` path, and no GA switch in any released
LiteLLM version — the OpenAI realtime WS provider hardcodes it. (Contrast:
the `XAIRealtime` subclass overrides `_get_additional_headers` to drop the
Beta header, and the Azure provider has a `LITELLM_AZURE_REALTIME_PROTOCOL`
GA/beta switch — the OpenAI provider has neither.)

This patch makes the OpenAI provider behave like the `XAIRealtime`
precedent: `_get_additional_headers` returns ONLY the `Authorization`
header. The OpenWhispr api `?intent=` strip (apps/api/src/routes/realtime.ts)
handles the URL-level half of the GA shape; this patch handles the
header-level half.

SCOPE
=====
Affects ONLY the `litellm` realtime backend (`REALTIME_BACKEND=litellm`,
the default). The `direct` backend bypasses LiteLLM entirely and never
needs this patch.

STALE BYTECODE GOTCHA
=====================
The LiteLLM base image ships PRE-COMPILED `.pyc` files. CPython uses
hash-based, `UNCHECKED` `.pyc` invalidation for them — it never re-checks
the `.py` source. A `sed` on the source therefore SILENTLY NO-OPS unless
the corresponding `__pycache__/*.pyc` is also deleted. The Dockerfile
drops every `__pycache__` tree after the sed. If you ever apply this
patch by another means, you MUST also clear the bytecode cache.

RE-APPLYING ON LITELLM BUMPS
============================
This patch is applied by `compose/litellm/Dockerfile` via a line-anchored
`sed` against `/app/litellm/llms/openai/realtime/handler.py`. On every
LiteLLM image bump:
  1. Re-pin the base image tag in compose/litellm/Dockerfile.
  2. Rebuild: `docker compose build litellm`.
  3. The Dockerfile's post-patch grep assertion FAILS the build if the
     anchored line is gone (LiteLLM refactored the method) — at which
     point this patch must be re-derived against the new source.
Track upstream for a native GA switch (LiteLLM issue/PR search:
"OpenAI realtime GA", "_get_additional_headers OpenAI-Beta"); when one
lands, this patch is retired in favour of config.

TARGET FILE (LiteLLM 1.83.14)
=============================
  /app/litellm/llms/openai/realtime/handler.py

  def _get_additional_headers(self, api_key: str) -> dict:
      ...
      return {
          "Authorization": f"Bearer {api_key}",
          "OpenAI-Beta": "realtime=v1",          <-- LINE REMOVED BY PATCH
      }
